    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass. The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner read model, following the repository's established pattern for derived fields.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the Owner schema (placed after `ageBand`), documenting the `<TIER>_<AREA>` format and the four possible values. This drives generation of the `ownerSegment` field on `OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 A plain static helper (like its siblings `MembershipLevel`, `AgeBand`, `OwnerLocality`) with `forOwner(Owner)`:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `MembershipLevel.forOwner(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when the locality (from `OwnerLocality.forCustomerCode`) is a known region (`NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`), else `REGIONAL`.\n   - Reuses the existing membership-level and locality derivation rather than duplicating the region table or level logic.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` wiring `ownerSegment` to `OwnerSegment.forOwner(owner)`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one) pass.",
